From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:03:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: Add the A733 video output 1 clock unit

TCON TV1 of the A733, which feeds the DisplayPort transmitter, gets no
pixel clock until the VIDEO_OUT1_SYS block selects the eDP side as its
clock source and releases its clock gate (user manual sections 15.2.9.1
and 15.2.9.2).

Add a driver for the block. Its two registers hold a clock source select
per TCON TV, the HDMI or the eDP side, a clock gate per TCON TV and the
gate of the clock from TCON TV0 to HDMI, and no display route, so it is
a clock unit in the form of the DE2 clock unit rather than a display
driver like the R40 TCON TOP, which also routes the display. The device
tree chooses the source with assigned-clock-parents, and the TCON takes
its channel 1 clock from the gate.

Figure 15-18 of the user manual draws its registers as the DPSS top
registers of the video output 1 subsystem, so its bus clock and reset
are taken to be those of DPSS_TOP1 in the CCU, with the video output 1
gate of the AHB bus matrix. They are not measured on our boards.

Not covered: the CVBS clock sources and the HDMI PHY clock source of
TCON TV0.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the clock unit opened
the TCON and transmitter clocks of video output 1, and the stream
reached the sink at the pixel clock of the mode.

Assisted-by: LLM
